{"name":"Amourette Eternelle","hex":"#e0dfe8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amourette","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A petty love affair.","The love grass, or quaking grass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amourette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Senegalia riparia","blocks":[{"text":"Senegalia riparia, commonly known as catch & keep, calumbi, jurema-branca, acacia zarza, amourette, and fleur du ben-aimé, is a thorny flowering plant of the family Fabaceae. It is native to Hispaniola, Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands, the Lesser Antilles,Trinidad, and northern South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Senegalia_riparia_syn._Piptadenia_retusa.jpg/330px-Senegalia_riparia_syn._Piptadenia_retusa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senegalia_riparia","wikidata":"Q15535648"},{"title":"Éternelle","blocks":[{"text":"Éternelle is a French television miniseries. It was produced by Alizés Film (France) in a format of six episodes of 52 minutes, directed by Didier Delaître. It stars Claire Keim and was broadcast for the first time on M6 between July 30, 2009 and August 13, 2009 on prime time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/16/Eternelle_dvd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%89ternelle","wikidata":"Q3591949"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.4225},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p